{"reason":"completed","text":"Haan bhai, full flow token mil gaya — ab token lifecycle samajhte hain. Ye sab code se confirmed hai, kuch bhi assume nahi kar raha.

## Architecture: Token pair

| Token | Type | TTL (tera config) | Storage |
|---|---|---|---|
| **Access token** | JWT (HS256), claims: `sub`, `username`, `email`, `typ` | ~5 min (docs default 900s) | Memory mein, har request ke saath |
| **Refresh token** | Opaque random 32-byte string | ~30 days | DB mein sirf SHA-256 hash save hota hai |

Key point: **refresh token rotate hota hai** — har `/refresh` call pe naya refresh token milta hai aur purana turant invalid. Toh UI ko har refresh response mein naya token replace karna padega.

## UI logic (React/JS)

**1. Storage**
- Access token → memory (React state/context). `localStorage` mein mat daal, XSS se chori ho jaata hai.
- Refresh token → ideally `httpOnly` cookie (server set kare tab best). Abhi API JSON mein deta hai, toh frontend ke liye memory + fallback storage use karo.

**2. Har request pe**
```
Authorization: Bearer <access_token>
```

**3. 401 aaye toh — "silent refresh + retry"**
Ye core logic hai. Access token expire hona normal hai, error nahi — usko gracefully handle karna hai:

```js
// Pseudocode — axios example
axios.interceptors.response.use(
  (res) => res,
  async (err) => {
    const original = err.config;
    if (err.response?.status !== 401 || original._retried) {
      return Promise.reject(err);
    }
    original._retried = true; // infinite loop rokne ke liye

    try {
      const { data } = await axios.post("/api/auth/refresh", {
        refresh_token: store.getRefreshToken(),
      });
      store.setAccessToken(data.tokens.access_token);
      store.setRefreshToken(data.tokens.refresh_token); // rotation - naya save karo!
      original.headers.Authorization = `Bearer ${data.tokens.access_token}`;
      return axios(original); // original request retry
    } catch {
      store.clear();          // refresh bhi fail = logout
      router.push("/login");
      return Promise.reject(err);
    }
  }
);
```

**4. Optional: proactive refresh**
Response mein `expires_at` already milta hai. Isko use karke expiry se ~30-60s pehle hi refresh call kar sakte ho — phir user ko 401 dikhega hi nahi. But reactive (401 pe) bhi zaroor rakhna, kyunki tab tak token expire ho chuka hoga.

**5. Logout**
Refresh token revoke karo + storage clear. Warna 30 din tak wapas login nahi kar paoge bina OTP ke.

## Ek important cheez

Refresh token ko **access token ki tarah Authorization header mein kabhi mat bhejo** — sirf `/api/auth/refresh` body mein. Backend `typ` claim check karta hai, refresh token JWT hai hi nahi, toh reject ho jayega.

